        "notes": "Checked all five steps: SPD convex combinations have positive eigenvalues; the reader determinant-product expansion follows the actual multiplicative, transpose and triangular determinant statements. Jacobi and inverse differentiation apply on the invertible cone; trace cyclicity and the sum of squares give a strictly negative line second derivative for nonzero symmetric H. Two MVT applications yield strict concavity, with equality only for identical endpoints. p=1 and all 0<t<1 are covered; no arbitrary choice is used. The reader addition makes an immediately recoverable determinant identity explicit, rather than repairing a false claim."
