        "notes": "All four steps and exact direct supplier statements checked. The reader uses the statement square root A and derives det(A)>0, det(Sigma)=det(A)^2 and A^T Sigma^{-1} A=I from spectral and determinant laws. Product normal densities are Borel, integrate to one by finite Tonelli and product/Euclidean Lebesgue agreement; rational rectangles with finite box exhaustion identify the joint law. The affine map is a C1 diffeomorphism; applying nonnegative change of variables to indicator times phi identifies the pushforward on every Borel set. AC implies the cited countable choice hypotheses. p=1, arbitrary means and SPD covariances checked; singular covariances excluded. The square-root clarification expands routine finite-dimensional algebra; no false claim or substantial missing prerequisite found."
