      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-20",
        "notes": "All eight steps and all direct supplier statements checked. Strictly positive Gaussian terms make every responsibility and N_k positive; full affine span forces the weighted scatter to be SPD, including K=1. The finite positive categorical KL is in the correct direction alpha||rho, with equality exactly at rho=alpha. Weighted centering gives a strictly positive mean penalty off the weighted mean for each fixed covariance. The precision inverse ranges bijectively over SPD matrices; the strict log-det lemma plus a linear trace term is strictly concave, with derivative zero at S_k^{-1}. Its secant-slope argument gives a strict global maximum, hence joint attainment and uniqueness in the labeled parameter coordinates. No singular-scatter or zero-weight case is admitted. AC is retained for the KL suppliers and normalization. Reader changes are proof spacing only."
      }
