      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-20",
        "notes": "All seven steps and all 26 direct supplier interfaces checked. Relative openness of the SPD cone follows from the explicit Frobenius Cauchy-Schwarz estimate, giving Borel parameter domain and jointly measurable continuous Gaussian factors. Finite products and Tonelli normalize each complete-data fibre; every observed marginal and posterior atom is finite and positive. Thus posterior support is shared, directional KL current||candidate is finite, and both absolute log-density expectations are finite. Corrected the false outer sum in step 4.2 to the individual coordinate normalization sum_{z_j=1}^K gamma_{j,z_j}=1 for every j!=i; finite summation over all other labels then factors as a product of these unit sums and yields exactly the M-step Q. The attained maximizer and general EM identity give nondecrease; full affine span preserves SPD by induction through every finite T. K=1, repeated observations within a full-span sample, and equality at a fixed point are allowed. Rank-deficient data, zero weights, singular covariances and convergence claims are excluded. AC/countable-choice uses are explicit. No unmet prerequisite remains."
      }
