    "ex-lloyd-tie-sensitive-local-minima": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-k-means-objective",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $n,p$ be positive integers, let $1\\le K\\le n$, let $x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\in\\mathbb R^p$ be observed vectors, and let $\\mu_1,\\ldots,\\mu_K\\in\\mathbb R^p$ be centers. A labeling is a vector $z=(z_1,\\ldots,z_n)\\in\\{1,\\ldots,K\\}^n$, and its $k$th cluster is $C_k(z):=\\{i:z_i=k\\}$. For $v=(v_1,\\ldots,v_p)\\in\\mathbb R^p$, set $\\|v\\|_2^2:=\\sum_{j=1}^p v_j^2$. The K-means objective is\n\n$$J(z,\\mu_1,\\ldots,\\mu_K):=\\sum_{i=1}^n\\|x_i-\\mu_{z_i}\\|_2^2=\\sum_{k=1}^K\\sum_{i\\in C_k(z)}\\|x_i-\\mu_k\\|_2^2.$$\n\nAn empty cluster contributes zero to the sum.",
          "uses": [
            "1.3",
            "2.1",
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "alg-lloyd-k-means",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**Input.** Let $n,p$ be positive integers, let $1\\le K\\le n$, let $x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\in\\mathbb R^p$, and supply initial centers $\\mu_1^{(0)},\\ldots,\\mu_K^{(0)}\\in\\mathbb R^p$.\n\n**Initialization.** Assign each $x_i$ to a nearest initial center, choosing the smallest center index in a tie. Denote these labels by $z_i^{(0)}$.\n\n**Iteration.** For $t=0,1,2,\\ldots$:\n\n1. With the current centers fixed, assign each $x_i$ to a nearest center. If its current label $z_i^{(t)}$ is among the nearest-center indices, retain $z_i^{(t)}$; otherwise choose the smallest nearest-center index. Call the resulting labels $z_i^{(t+1)}$.\n2. For each nonempty cluster $C_k^{(t+1)}:=\\{i:z_i^{(t+1)}=k\\}$, set\n   $$\\mu_k^{(t+1)}:=\\frac{1}{|C_k^{(t+1)}|}\\sum_{i\\in C_k^{(t+1)}}x_i.$$\n   If $C_k^{(t+1)}$ is empty, set $\\mu_k^{(t+1)}:=\\mu_k^{(t)}$.\n3. If both $z^{(t+1)}=z^{(t)}$ and $\\mu^{(t+1)}=\\mu^{(t)}$, return these labels and centers. Otherwise continue with the updated labels and centers.\n\nThe procedure makes no global-minimization claim. Its termination under these tie rules is proved separately.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "1.3",
            "2.1",
            "2.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "d-1-1",
          "claim": "From initial centers $(0,11/10)$, the nearest labels are $(1,2,2,2)$: the respective comparisons are $0<121/100$, $1>1/100$, $4>81/100$, and $9>361/100$. The mean update gives centers $0$ and $(1+2+3)/3=2$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F2",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1-2",
          "claim": "From initial centers $(3,19/10)$, nearest labels are $(2,2,2,1)$: observations $0,1,2$ are strictly nearer $19/10$, while $3$ equals the first center. Their means become $3$ for cluster $1$ and $(0+1+2)/3=1$ for cluster $2$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-1-3",
          "claim": "From initial centers $(1/2,5/2)$, nearest labels are $(1,1,2,2)$. The means of these clusters are again $1/2$ and $5/2$, so labels and centers are unchanged and the procedure stops. The objective is $4(1/2)^2=1$.",
          "step": "1.3",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-2-1",
          "claim": "With centers $(0,2)$, observations $0,2,3$ keep labels $1,2,2$ by strict nearest comparisons; observation $1$ is at distance $1$ from each center and retains its current label $2$. The labels remain $(1,2,2,2)$, so their means remain $(0,2)$ and the procedure stops. The objective is $(0-0)^2+(1-2)^2+(2-2)^2+(3-2)^2=2$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-2-2",
          "claim": "With centers $(3,1)$, observations $0,1,3$ keep labels $2,2,1$ by strict nearest comparisons; observation $2$ is tied at distance $1$ and retains label $2$. The labels stay $(2,2,2,1)$, their means remain $(3,1)$, and the procedure stops. The objective is $(0-1)^2+(1-1)^2+(2-1)^2+(3-3)^2=2$.",
          "step": "2.2",
